# Claim

**1.** A diesel fuel composition comprising:

a major amount of a diesel fuel boiling in the diesel fuel range; and

a minor detergent-effective amount of an additive combination comprising:

**(a)** a quaternized nitrogen detergent additive formed by reacting a tertiary amine having the structure:

$$R^1-N(R^2)(R^3)$$

wherein R¹ is a hydrocarbyl group having from about 8 to about 500 carbon atoms, optionally substituted with one or more polar functional groups selected from hydroxyl, ester, amide, or amino groups, and wherein R² and R³ are independently selected from C₁ to C₄ alkyl groups, or R² and R³ together with the nitrogen atom form a 5- or 6-membered heterocyclic ring;

with a quaternizing agent selected from the group consisting of a hydrocarbyl-substituted epoxide, a hydrocarbyl-substituted carbonate, a dihydrocarbyl sulfate, a hydrocarbyl halide, or a hydrocarbyl ester of a hydrocarbylsulfonic acid, to form a quaternary ammonium salt; and

**(b)** a phenolic Mannich reaction product represented by the formula:

$$\left[ \text{Ar(OH)}(R^4)_x - \text{CH}_2 - N(R^5)(R^6) \right]$$

wherein:

Ar is a substituted or unsubstituted aromatic or polyaromatic nucleus;

R⁴ is a hydrocarbyl-based substituent having from about 30 to about 400 carbon atoms, derived from a polyolefin selected from the group consisting of polyisobutylene, polypropylene, and copolymers thereof, attached directly to the aromatic ring;

x is an integer of 1 or 2;

R⁵ and R⁶ are independently selected from hydrogen, C₁ to C₆ alkyl groups, hydroxyalkyl groups, or aminoalkyl groups, or R⁵ and R⁶ together with the nitrogen atom form a saturated heterocyclic ring containing from 5 to 7 ring members and optionally a second heteroatom selected from oxygen or nitrogen;

wherein the weight ratio of component (a) to component (b) ranges from about 1:10 to about 10:1.
